From bacbf9f13e53e66252d9974c5f4271259ecddfc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeltaVector1 <DeltaVector1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:04:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/33] Settle on 128 in flight; 192 buys nothing and costs
 five times the errors

Full-batch cycle times, which is the metric that sets the step time:

  step 6  137.4 min  78.3% error  0.0530   256 in flight, 24 tunnels, no compression
  step 7  118.3 min  18.9% error  0.0889   128, compression landed mid-batch
  step 8   82.6 min   5.1% error  0.1065   128, 24 tunnels, bounded timeouts
  step 9   84.8 min  25.9% error  0.0736   192, 48 tunnels, bounded timeouts

192 in flight looked good on a mid-batch window (23.18/min) and on engine
concurrency (26 -> 46), and both were real, but neither survived a full batch.
It finished no faster and put the error rate back to 25.9%. Extra in-flight
past what the path sustains turns into timeouts, and a timed-out rollout is
work the engines did and then threw away.

Step 8's configuration is the best measured: 82.6 minutes, 5.1% error, and the
run's best effective reward at 0.1065.

The 48 tunnels stay. They cost nothing, they made no difference at 128 in
flight (14.20 against 13.95/min), and they leave headroom if the path improves.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wiESxhziDrnsLnG9aizTd
---
 configs/china/orchestrator.x24.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/china/orchestrator.x24.toml b/configs/china/orchestrator.x24.toml
index d87154a..7760116 100644
--- a/configs/china/orchestrator.x24.toml
+++ b/configs/china/orchestrator.x24.toml
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ max_steps = 200
 seq_len = 16384
 batch_size = 1024
 group_size = 16
-max_inflight_rollouts = 192
+max_inflight_rollouts = 128
 # 4, not 2: batches go out over ZMQ fire-and-forget, so a trainer restart
 # loses whatever was in flight. With a tight cap the orchestrator then holds
 # for a policy the restarted trainer cannot publish and both sides wait
